  "final": "Done. `GET /files/<name>` now returns the signed-in caller's own file as an attachment (`application/octet-stream`, `Content-Disposition: attachment`, `nosniff`). I ran `python3 -m unittest` and all 8 tests pass.\n\n- **Boundary:** a user can download only files in their own `$UPLOAD_ROOT/<user>/` directory. `storage.read` (in `files_app/storage.py`) enforces this per file. It applies `valid_name`, rejects NUL bytes, resolves the real path, and requires that path to sit directly in the user's directory.\n- **Failures:** a missing file, another user's file, a traversal attempt or a bad name all return 404. No token returns 401.\n- **Negative-test check:** I temporarily removed the name and containment guards. `test_download_traversal_denied` then errored, and it passes again with the guards restored.\n- **Tests and README:** I added 5 tests (owner download, no auth, cross-user, traversal, missing file) and a README line.\n- **Not run:** I did not run `ult scan`.",
